{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":false},"description":"Compare two local files byte-for-byte and explain what changed, for any file type (firmware dumps, ECU calibration files, app or driver updates, data blobs), not only executables. Returns both files' SHA-256 and size, whether they are identical, the size delta, the count and fraction of changed bytes, the overall changed offset range, a summary (how many bytes were zeroed, filled with 0xFF, or otherwise modified), and a bounded list of contiguous changed regions \u2014 each with its file offset, length, a kind (zeroed/filled/modified) and before/after value samples read as little-endian words of the chosen width. Regions are coalesced by a caller gap and bounded by max_regions. Reads both files once (up to 256 MiB each) WITHOUT executing them, without network access and without writing files; the report is bounded to 8 MiB. It does no format-aware labeling: it reports where and how bytes differ, not named maps, fields or functions. Only the shorter length is compared; extra trailing bytes are reported as size_delta.","inputSchema":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","additionalProperties":false,"examples":[{"base_path":"/artifacts/original.bin","target_path":"/artifacts/modified.bin"},{"base_path":"/artifacts/app-v1","target_path":"/artifacts/app-v2","word_size":4}],"properties":{"base_path":{"description":"Absolute path to the baseline file","minLength":1,"pattern":"^[^\\x00]*$","type":"string"},"max_regions":{"default":500,"description":"Maximum changed regions returned before truncation","maximum":5000,"minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"region_gap":{"default":32,"description":"Maximum run of equal bytes that still merges two changes into one region","maximum":4096,"minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"samples_per_region":{"default":6,"description":"Maximum before/after value samples listed per region","maximum":64,"minimum":0,"type":